[ti:Nine New Members and a Wider PyTorch Ecosystem]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: If you work on a PyTorch backend, a foundation membership announcement may sound distant from your code.
[00:00.00]Ava：如果你在开发 PyTorch 后端，基金会的新成员公告可能让你觉得离代码很远。
[00:07.69]But this one sits beside updates for tiny CPUs, cloud accelerators, TPUs, and production serving.
[00:07.69]但这次公告还涉及小型 CPU、云加速器、TPU 和生产环境中的模型服务。
[00:14.86]That range makes the membership story worth a closer look.
[00:14.86]这样的覆盖范围让这则入会消息值得细看。
[00:19.50]Brian: The PyTorch Foundation announced 9 new members at PyTorch Conference North America 2026.
[00:19.50]Brian：PyTorch 基金会在 2026 年北美 PyTorch 大会上宣布新增 9 名成员。
[00:26.06]It presents itself as a shared hub for open source AI across the stack.
[00:26.06]基金会将自己定位为贯穿技术栈的开源 AI 共享平台。
[00:31.35]The engineering question is how work moves between projects, hardware, and deployed systems.
[00:31.35]工程上的问题是，成果如何在项目、硬件和已部署系统之间流转。
[00:38.55]Ava: So let's make that concrete.
[00:38.55]Ava：那就说具体些。
[00:40.40]Who joined, and do the membership levels tell us anything technical?
[00:40.40]谁加入了？会员级别能说明什么技术问题吗？
[00:44.91]I wouldn't treat a Platinum label as proof that a new backend works for my model.
[00:44.91]我不会把白金会员身份当作新后端能运行我的模型的证明。
[00:50.63]Brian: The 3 Platinum members are Nebius, Nscale, and Shopify Inc.
[00:50.63]Brian：3 家白金会员是 Nebius、Nscale 和 Shopify Inc.。
[00:55.44]The 2 Silver members are LightSeek Foundation and Lablup Inc.
[00:55.44]2 家白银会员是 LightSeek Foundation 和 Lablup Inc.。
[01:00.41]The 4 Associate members are SKOPOS INDIA FOUNDATION, Siksha ‘O’ Anusandhan, Messiah University, and Valencia College.
[01:00.41]4 家联系会员是 SKOPOS INDIA FOUNDATION、Siksha ‘O’ Anusandhan、Messiah University 和 Valencia College。
[01:09.94]Those are membership categories; the article makes separate claims about technical work.
[01:09.94]这些是会员类别；文章对技术工作另有论述。
[01:17.46]Ava: That mix matters.
[01:17.46]Ava：这种成员构成很重要。
[01:18.65]Companies working on infrastructure or applications sit alongside foundations and educational institutions.
[01:18.65]从事基础设施或应用开发的公司，与基金会和教育机构同在其中。
[01:26.13]If they bring different workloads to a shared project, framework decisions may have to answer to more kinds of users.
[01:26.13]如果他们把不同工作负载带入共同的项目，框架设计就可能需要回应更多类型用户的需求。
[01:34.32]That's a plausible benefit of membership, not a reported performance result.
[01:34.32]这是会员机制可能带来的好处，不是已报告的性能结果。
[01:39.98]Brian: The Foundation says open source AI now advances through research, models, infrastructure, hardware, and production at the same time.
[01:39.98]Brian：基金会表示，如今开源 AI 的进展同时发生在研究、模型、基础设施、硬件和生产应用各环节。
[01:49.61]It supports PyTorch and projects including vLLM, DeepSpeed, Ray, Helion, and Safetensors.
[01:49.61]它支持 PyTorch，以及 vLLM、DeepSpeed、Ray、Helion 和 Safetensors 等项目。
[01:56.11]The claim is that a shared home helps advances travel between those parts.
[01:56.11]其主张是，共同的平台有助于各环节共享进展。
[02:01.86]Ava: From an engineering point of view, I can see the attraction.
[02:01.86]Ava：从工程角度看，我能理解其吸引力。
[02:06.02]Imagine a model trained in PyTorch, adapted to one accelerator, then served through another project.
[02:06.02]想象一个模型在 PyTorch 中训练，适配某种加速器，再通过另一个项目提供服务。
[02:12.96]Each boundary gives you a place where a useful improvement can get stuck.
[02:12.96]每跨越一道边界，实用的改进都可能卡在那里。
[02:18.02]Does the announcement show how that sharing works?
[02:18.02]公告说明了这种共享如何运作吗？
[02:21.84]Brian: It gives examples, rather than a universal rule for compatibility.
[02:21.84]Brian：它给出了例子，而不是通用的兼容性规则。
[02:26.78]The member news spans on-device inference, new accelerator backends, compiler work, and a production learning loop.
[02:26.78]成员动态涵盖端侧推理、新加速器后端、编译器工作，以及生产环境中的学习闭环。
[02:35.39]We can inspect those examples one by one.
[02:35.39]我们可以逐一看这些例子。
[02:38.46]The scope of each claim matters as much as the headline.
[02:38.46]每项说法的适用范围和标题同样重要。
[02:43.00]Ava: Let's start at the small-device end.
[02:43.00]Ava：先从小设备说起。
[02:45.62]Training is familiar, but getting from a PyTorch model to an Arm Cortex-M CPU is a different engineering problem.
[02:45.62]训练大家都熟悉，但让 PyTorch 模型跑在 Arm Cortex-M CPU 上是另一个工程问题。
[02:53.83]What does ExecuTorch add here?
[02:53.83]ExecuTorch 在这里提供了什么？
[02:56.36]Brian: The article says ExecuTorch provides a direct path from PyTorch training to on-device inference.
[02:56.36]Brian：文章称，ExecuTorch 提供了从 PyTorch 训练到设备端推理的直接路径。
[03:04.93]Its Cortex-M backend runs PyTorch models directly on Arm Cortex-M CPUs, with Arm CMSIS-NN acceleration.
[03:04.93]它的 Cortex-M 后端借助 Arm CMSIS-NN 加速，让 PyTorch 模型直接运行在 Arm Cortex-M CPU 上。
[03:14.12]It supports Scalar, DSP, and MVE/Helium capability tiers from a single workflow.
[03:14.12]单一工作流支持 Scalar、DSP 和 MVE/Helium 三档能力。
[03:21.27]I'd stop at that compatibility and workflow claim rather than infer a latency figure.
[03:21.27]我只会认可其兼容性和工作流方面的说法，不会据此推断延迟数值。
[03:29.20]Ava: The single workflow is the part I'd notice as a maintainer.
[03:29.20]Ava：作为维护者，我会留意这个单一工作流。
[03:33.16]Those capability tiers differ, so a common route could reduce the number of separate paths a team has to manage.
[03:33.16]这些能力档位各不相同，统一路径可能减少团队需要管理的独立流程。
[03:40.68]I'm reading that as an engineering implication, not a measured claim in the announcement.
[03:40.68]这是我的工程推断，不是公告给出的测量结论。
[03:47.00]Brian: What does that buy you?
[03:47.00]Brian：这能带来什么？
[03:48.53]It links the training side to on-device inference while naming the CPU capabilities the backend supports.
[03:48.53]它将训练与设备端推理衔接起来，并明确了后端支持的 CPU 能力。
[03:55.51]It gives us no basis to promise that every PyTorch model runs unchanged, so we'd still check the supported path for a real deployment.
[03:55.51]这不足以保证所有 PyTorch 模型都能原样运行，实际部署仍需核对支持范围。
[04:04.78]Ava: At the other end of the hardware range, there's TorchNeuron for AWS Trainium.
[04:04.78]Ava：硬件范围的另一端，是面向 AWS Trainium 的 TorchNeuron。
[04:10.02]The announcement describes a single configuration change for running PyTorch workloads.
[04:10.02]公告称，只需更改一处配置就能运行 PyTorch 工作负载。
[04:15.94]That sounds convenient, but a configuration switch alone wouldn't tell me which development styles remain available.
[04:15.94]听起来很方便，但仅靠一个配置开关，我无法判断还能使用哪些开发方式。
[04:24.18]Brian: It says TorchNeuron is an open source native PyTorch backend for AWS Trainium, including Amazon EC2 Trn2 and Trn3 instances.
[04:24.18]Brian：公告称，TorchNeuron 是面向 AWS Trainium 的开源原生 PyTorch 后端，支持 Amazon EC2 Trn2 和 Trn3 实例。
[04:34.34]It supports eager execution and torch.compile, plus PyTorch APIs such as DTensor and torch.distributed and libraries such as TorchTitan.
[04:34.34]它支持即时执行和 torch.compile，也支持 DTensor、torch.distributed 等 PyTorch API，以及 TorchTitan 等库。
[04:45.48]Those details connect the device path to workflows developers already use.
[04:45.48]这些细节表明，这条设备路径能接入开发者现有的工作流。
[04:51.89]Ava: So the single configuration change is the entry point.
[04:51.89]Ava：所以，更改一处配置只是入口。
[04:55.85]The more substantial claim is support for both eager and compiled execution, distributed APIs, and TorchTitan.
[04:55.85]更实质的主张是，它同时支持即时执行与编译执行、分布式 API 和 TorchTitan。
[05:03.91]I still wouldn't turn that into a promise that every workload needs no other work.
[05:03.91]但我仍不会因此保证每种工作负载都无需额外调整。
[05:10.27]Brian: That's a useful distinction.
[05:10.27]Brian：这个区分很有用。
[05:12.15]The article says researchers and practitioners can experiment and run PyTorch workloads with that change, across workflows from research to production deployment.
[05:12.15]文章说，有了这项变化，研究人员和从业者可以在从研究到生产部署的各类流程中试验和运行 PyTorch 工作负载。
[05:23.06]It doesn't establish a per-model migration guarantee.
[05:23.06]但这并不保证每个模型都能迁移。
[05:26.63]For a backend engineer, that means checking the exact PyTorch features a workload uses.
[05:26.63]对后端工程师来说，这意味着要核查工作负载具体用了哪些 PyTorch 功能。
[05:32.84]Ava: Now take TPUs. Google announced TorchTPU as native PyTorch for TPU developers.
[05:32.84]Ava：再看 TPU。Google 宣布推出 TorchTPU，让 TPU 开发者原生使用 PyTorch。
[05:38.91]If I'm already using PyTorch, I'd ask whether I can keep the surrounding serving and orchestration tools, not only move the model's compute.
[05:38.91]如果我已经在用 PyTorch，我会问：除了迁移模型计算，现有的服务和编排工具还能继续用吗？
[05:50.16]Brian: The stated aim is deployment on TPUs with minimal code changes.
[05:50.16]Brian：其宣称的目标是只需少量代码改动，就能在 TPU 上部署。
[05:55.67]The announcement also names access to vLLM, SGLang, Ray, and LLM-d.
[05:55.67]公告还提到可使用 vLLM、SGLang、Ray 和 LLM-d。
[06:01.53]That broadens the story beyond running an operation on a device.
[06:01.53]这就不只是让设备执行某项运算了。
[06:07.14]It connects the backend to projects a team may use around deployment.
[06:07.14]它把后端与团队部署时可能使用的项目连接起来。
[06:13.52]Ava: That changes the picture.
[06:13.52]Ava：这让情况不一样了。
[06:15.16]A device backend is easier to evaluate when you can see how it fits the rest of the workflow.
[06:15.16]看得出设备后端如何融入整个流程，才更容易评估它。
[06:21.26]Still, minimal code changes is a broad phrase.
[06:21.26]不过，“少量代码改动”说得很宽泛。
[06:24.27]We'd have to test our own model and tools before treating it as a migration estimate.
[06:24.27]要估算迁移工作量，还得先测试我们自己的模型和工具。
[06:30.19]Brian: The IBM Spyre example looks at a different boundary: compiler maintenance.
[06:30.19]Brian：IBM Spyre 的例子关注另一个环节：编译器维护。
[06:35.54]IBM's software stack extends PyTorch's Inductor compiler and native runtime.
[06:35.54]IBM 的软件栈扩展了 PyTorch 的 Inductor 编译器和原生运行时。
[06:41.03]The announcement says Spyre-specific compiler code was reduced by 7x while performance stayed at parity on the tested workloads.
[06:41.03]公告称，Spyre 专用编译器代码缩减了 7 倍，而在受测工作负载上的性能保持同等水平。
[06:50.29]The tested-workload qualifier limits what that performance statement covers.
[06:50.29]“受测工作负载”限定了这项性能结论的适用范围。
[06:56.13]Ava: When I hear about a 7x reduction in device-specific compiler code, I think about how much custom logic has to track upstream changes.
[06:56.13]Ava：听到设备专用编译器代码缩减了 7 倍，我会想到：需要跟进上游变化的定制逻辑少了多少？
[07:04.91]That's an inference about maintenance pressure.
[07:04.91]这是对维护压力的推断。
[07:08.01]It isn't evidence that every model gets faster, and the announcement doesn't make that claim.
[07:08.01]这不能证明每个模型都会变快，公告也没有这样声称。
[07:14.50]Brian: The same example says AI-assisted development enabled support for thousands of models with 44 adapters and approximately 10,000 lines of code.
[07:14.50]Brian：同一个例子还说，借助 AI 辅助开发，44 个适配器和约 10,000 行代码就支持了数千个模型。
[07:24.48]It also mentions hardware-agnostic vLLM integration and continuous testing against upstream PyTorch updates.
[07:24.48]它还提到与硬件无关的 vLLM 集成，以及持续针对上游 PyTorch 更新进行测试。
[07:32.07]Together, those details describe how IBM is trying to keep its device path aligned with the wider ecosystem.
[07:32.07]这些细节共同说明了 IBM 如何努力让其设备支持与更广泛的生态保持同步。
[07:40.00]Ava: I like that continuous testing detail.
[07:40.00]Ava：我很看重持续测试这一点。
[07:42.66]When upstream code moves, a backend can drift even if its first release works.
[07:42.66]上游代码一变，即使后端初版运行正常，也可能逐渐脱节。
[07:48.11]Here we have a concrete maintenance practice alongside a code-size claim.
[07:48.11]这里除了代码量的说法，还有一项具体的维护做法。
[07:53.22]Neither tells us how an untested workload performs, so the qualification stays in view.
[07:53.22]两者都不能说明未测试的工作负载表现如何，所以仍要记住这个限定。
[07:59.65]Brian: The application example comes from Shopify.
[07:59.65]Brian：应用方面的例子来自 Shopify。
[08:02.91]It built a continual learning loop with PyTorch and vLLM.
[08:02.91]它用 PyTorch 和 vLLM 建立了持续学习闭环。
[08:07.24]The article describes production failures being compressed into model weights every day.
[08:07.24]文章描述说，生产环境中的失败案例每天都会被压缩进模型权重。
[08:13.91]It says this beats frontier-model quality and cuts serving costs by 96%.
[08:13.91]文章称，这样做的质量超过前沿模型，服务成本降低了 96%。
[08:19.37]That's a striking claim about Shopify's case.
[08:19.37]这是对 Shopify 这个案例相当引人注目的说法。
[08:23.14]Ava: How far can we take that? The 96% number belongs to that Shopify case study.
[08:23.14]Ava：这个结论能推广多远？96% 这个数字只属于 Shopify 的案例研究。
[08:28.38]We shouldn't transfer it to another workload without more context.
[08:28.38]没有更多背景，就不该把它套用到其他工作负载。
[08:32.93]The same applies to the quality comparison: we'd need its evaluation context before using it to predict another application's results.
[08:32.93]质量对比也是如此：要用它预测其他应用的结果，得先了解其评估背景。
[08:42.52]Brian: The practical question is which part of the loop you can reuse.
[08:42.52]Brian：实际要问的是，这个闭环的哪些部分可以复用。
[08:46.90]PyTorch and vLLM are named together in the case study.
[08:46.90]案例研究同时提到了 PyTorch 和 vLLM。
[08:50.66]The description links production failures to daily updates in model weights and reports a serving-cost outcome.
[08:50.66]文中将生产环境中的失败案例与模型权重的每日更新联系起来，并报告了服务成本的变化。
[08:58.38]It doesn't establish a general recipe for every product.
[08:58.38]它并未给出适用于所有产品的通用方案。
[09:02.62]Ava: The member statements help explain why these examples sit together.
[09:02.62]Ava：各成员的表态有助于解释为什么这些例子会放在一起。
[09:07.52]Lablup says PyTorch workloads run on Backend.AI every day.
[09:07.52]Lablup 表示，PyTorch 工作负载每天都在 Backend.AI 上运行。
[09:11.77]Nscale talks about the framework and the data center as one problem, and about Ray running work across thousands of GPUs.
[09:11.77]Nscale 把框架和数据中心视为同一个问题，并谈到 Ray 如何将工作分配到数千块 GPU 上运行。
[09:20.62]Those are member perspectives, not independent measurements.
[09:20.62]这些是成员的观点，并非独立测量结果。
[09:25.36]Brian: Nebius points to the path from experimentation to production.
[09:25.36]Brian：Nebius 关注从实验走向生产的路径。
[09:29.80]LightSeek Foundation stresses open infrastructure for efficient inference.
[09:29.80]LightSeek Foundation 强调支持高效推理的开放基础设施。
[09:35.19]Each has a different entry point, but the Foundation's stated goal is a vendor-neutral home for training, optimizing, serving, orchestrating, and running models across chips and clouds.
[09:35.19]各方的切入点不同，但基金会宣称的目标是建立一个不依赖特定供应商的平台，支持跨芯片和云平台训练、优化、服务、编排和运行模型。
[09:48.66]That explains the broad membership mix.
[09:48.66]这解释了成员构成为什么如此多元。
[09:51.85]Ava: Where does this leave us?
[09:51.85]Ava：这对我们意味着什么？
[09:53.49]The conference brings together people working on training, inference, kernel engineering, and responsible AI.
[09:53.49]这场大会汇聚了从事训练、推理、内核工程和负责任 AI 的人。
[10:00.62]I'd watch how the named backends and project integrations develop.
[10:00.62]我会关注这些点名的后端和项目集成后续如何发展。
[10:04.94]The announcement gives examples of progress; it doesn't establish a release schedule for what follows.
[10:04.94]公告列举了进展，但没有给出后续的发布计划。
[10:11.97]Brian: The useful takeaway is that the Foundation added 9 members, while the ecosystem news ranges from ExecuTorch on Cortex-M to TorchNeuron, TorchTPU, IBM Spyre, and Shopify's learning loop.
[10:11.97]Brian：关键是基金会新增了9名成员；生态方面的消息涵盖 Cortex-M 上的 ExecuTorch、TorchNeuron、TorchTPU、IBM Spyre，以及 Shopify 的学习闭环。
[10:26.35]For each example, keep the stated scope and qualifiers attached.
[10:26.35]谈到每个例子时，都要保留其适用范围和限定条件。
[10:31.32]That gives us a sound basis for engineering questions. Thanks for listening.
[10:31.32]这为我们探讨工程问题提供了可靠依据。感谢收听。
